1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,400
Episode 2

2
00:00:10,760 --> 00:00:12,080
Hey, you guys!

3
00:00:12,420 --> 00:00:17,280
Is everybody gonna be ready for that big
party after we kick Kaido's sorry butt?

4
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:19,330
Yeah!

5
00:00:19,413 --> 00:00:20,243
Move it!

6
00:00:20,326 --> 00:00:21,500
You're in my way!

7
00:00:34,460 --> 00:00:36,560
Look, it's Draghi!

8
00:00:36,720 --> 00:00:39,400
I already said I got dibs on Kaido.

9
00:00:39,920 --> 00:00:41,980
It's personal lanes.

10
00:00:44,960 --> 00:00:46,360
Sure it is.

11
00:00:57,440 --> 00:01:01,620
If I were you, I'd go brush my
hair and wash my face, Kaido.

12
00:01:01,900 --> 00:01:06,960
Because I'm taking that head of yours
and putting it on the bow of my ship.

13
00:01:07,340 --> 00:01:10,177
Yeah, he's going to pay
for making Killa so happy.

14
00:01:10,260 --> 00:01:11,613
That's not cool at all.

15
00:01:11,820 --> 00:01:14,897
Now we all got to be
happy so he feels at home.

16
00:01:14,980 --> 00:01:16,840
No, you don't

17
00:01:25,220 --> 00:01:29,340
See you later straw
hats if you can keep up

18
00:01:35,660 --> 00:01:38,520
Please they're having fun

19
00:01:41,100 --> 00:01:41,930
Gene Bay!

20
00:01:42,260 --> 00:01:43,731
You know what to do next!

21
00:01:43,920 --> 00:01:46,155
Don't let us fall behind Jaggy's ship!

22
00:01:48,100 --> 00:01:50,720
Having a race, are we? Sounds good!

23
00:01:50,920 --> 00:01:51,920
Leave it to me!

24
00:01:52,200 --> 00:01:55,906
I'll catch that rascal's ship
and we'll beat him to the island!

25
00:01:56,020 --> 00:01:57,260
Now hold on tight!

26
00:02:03,400 --> 00:02:04,500
Oh, yeah!

27
00:02:04,880 --> 00:02:05,980
Here he comes!

28
00:02:06,280 --> 00:02:08,180
Show us what you've got, Jinbe!

29
00:02:08,420 --> 00:02:10,420
We're gonna smoke those guys easy!

30
00:02:14,880 --> 00:02:17,300
Better not lose to anyone else, Kaido!

31
00:02:17,580 --> 00:02:18,920
I'm on my way!

32
00:02:19,240 --> 00:02:20,220
Get ready!

33
00:02:28,380 --> 00:02:31,060
Let's play on the card,

34
00:02:40,760 --> 00:02:42,300
Don't get up!

35
00:02:51,260 --> 00:02:53,540
I'm not Shut it up!

36
00:03:10,360 --> 00:03:11,877
I'll see

37
00:03:11,960 --> 00:03:18,960
you

38
00:03:24,720 --> 00:03:26,320
next time.

39
00:03:26,460 --> 00:03:27,780
Dreamin' on!

40
00:03:57,300 --> 00:03:59,160
We shall meet again shortly.

41
00:03:59,400 --> 00:04:01,106
See you at the back entrance.

42
00:04:05,440 --> 00:04:06,540
Neat, neat!

43
00:04:10,800 --> 00:04:13,500
Sir Law, it's in your hands!

44
00:04:13,720 --> 00:04:14,640
Guide us!

45
00:04:15,500 --> 00:04:16,820
Submerge the ship!

46
00:04:17,240 --> 00:04:18,420
Yes, sir!

47
00:04:26,200 --> 00:04:30,960
Penguin, adjust our trim 30 degrees
Adjusting trim 30 degrees Got it

48
00:04:35,080 --> 00:04:39,860
Sustain a depth of 100 meters Captain,
can you confirm our final destination?

49
00:04:40,240 --> 00:04:45,640
To the rear shore of Onigashima
Go full speed ahead Aye, aye, sir

50
00:04:53,460 --> 00:04:58,557
we are drawing near stay sharp everyone we

51
00:04:58,640 --> 00:05:00,437
don't know what to expect from here on out

52
00:05:00,520 --> 00:05:04,077
there could be an ambush
at any instant haven't

53
00:05:04,160 --> 00:05:06,572
lost your touch in all these years i hope

54
00:05:07,460 --> 00:05:11,740
just the opposite my friend why else
would i endure two decades of pain

55
00:05:13,660 --> 00:05:14,777
Ha ha ha!

56
00:05:14,860 --> 00:05:15,857
Grim, but I'll take it.

57
00:05:15,940 --> 00:05:17,640
Let's put an end to this.

58
00:05:18,220 --> 00:05:19,050
Of course.

59
00:05:30,280 --> 00:05:31,780
Staring us down, huh?

60
00:05:47,020 --> 00:05:49,380
So this is Onigashima.

61
00:05:52,260 --> 00:05:54,460
It's bigger than I expected.

62
00:05:55,320 --> 00:05:56,700
The enemy's stronghold.

63
00:05:57,000 --> 00:05:57,980
It's massive!

64
00:05:58,360 --> 00:05:59,900
Kaido really lives here?

65
00:06:00,380 --> 00:06:02,300
Look, King, through the screen.

66
00:06:03,460 --> 00:06:05,957
Yes, they're having a
party just as we'd hoped.

67
00:06:06,040 --> 00:06:09,216
They aren't on the lookout
for an enemy attack at all.

68
00:06:09,320 --> 00:06:12,438
I suppose they haven't yet
received Conjido's report.

69
00:06:12,580 --> 00:06:16,037
Or perhaps they have received it,
but deemed it inconsequential.

70
00:06:16,120 --> 00:06:18,777
Either way, their
complacency is our blessing.

71
00:06:18,860 --> 00:06:21,566
Now, we will continue
forward with confidence.

72
00:06:21,980 --> 00:06:24,745
We shall strike before
they know what hit them.

73
00:06:27,520 --> 00:06:29,497
The castle's in the center, right?

74
00:06:29,580 --> 00:06:31,960
Inside that giant skull. That's right.

75
00:06:32,140 --> 00:06:33,905
Hard to see from here, though.

76
00:06:34,060 --> 00:06:37,597
I thought it'd be closer to the
shore, but we still got a ways to go.

77
00:06:37,680 --> 00:06:39,940
I don't think they've noticed us.

78
00:06:40,180 --> 00:06:42,239
Better haul ass while we still can.

79
00:06:42,860 --> 00:06:44,780
Hey, it's a guard!

80
00:06:45,460 --> 00:06:46,460
What's that?

81
00:06:46,860 --> 00:06:48,740
They look like ships.

82
00:06:49,640 --> 00:06:50,900
Are you seeing this?

83
00:06:51,640 --> 00:06:52,470
Huh?

84
00:06:52,553 --> 00:06:53,383
That can't be right.

85
00:06:53,466 --> 00:06:55,537
I didn't hear nothing about no boats.

86
00:06:55,620 --> 00:06:57,640
Why don't you take a little nap?

87
00:06:58,660 --> 00:06:59,660
Special attack.

88
00:06:59,960 --> 00:07:01,220
Green Star, go!

89
00:07:08,360 --> 00:07:09,190
Ahhhh!

90
00:07:11,240 --> 00:07:12,420
That's sleep grass.

91
00:07:16,540 --> 00:07:17,440
Hold on.

92
00:07:17,820 --> 00:07:20,467
Weren't there guards
over there a moment ago?

93
00:07:28,260 --> 00:07:30,000
Looks like they're out cold.

94
00:07:30,220 --> 00:07:31,691
Wonder how that happened.

95
00:07:32,060 --> 00:07:33,800
You sleep tight now.

96
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:41,824
I understand the plan, but there's
one thing that's troubling me.

97
00:07:42,140 --> 00:07:44,997
Although it's reassuring that
our numbers are so great,

98
00:07:45,080 --> 00:07:47,197
we have an awful lot of ships out here.

99
00:07:47,280 --> 00:07:51,986
If we leave them moored this way, the
enemy will take notice and guess our plan.

100
00:07:52,180 --> 00:07:54,533
Everyone disembark and ready your tools!

101
00:07:59,260 --> 00:08:00,600
What are they up to?

102
00:08:00,900 --> 00:08:02,577
Wait, don't tell me they're gonna...

103
00:08:02,660 --> 00:08:04,060
Seek the ships!

104
00:08:14,300 --> 00:08:15,717
Is this part of the plan?

105
00:08:15,800 --> 00:08:16,977
Because nobody told me!

106
00:08:17,060 --> 00:08:17,890
What are they doing?

107
00:08:17,973 --> 00:08:19,411
They were tired on those!

108
00:08:24,120 --> 00:08:25,260
Why'd you do that?

109
00:08:25,460 --> 00:08:27,931
Because you were trying to hide the ships?

110
00:08:28,020 --> 00:08:30,844
How the heck are you
supposed to sail them home?

111
00:08:31,040 --> 00:08:32,334
What are you thinking?

112
00:08:32,620 --> 00:08:34,217
You're going to get stuck here!

113
00:08:34,300 --> 00:08:37,124
If things go south,
there'll be no turning back!

114
00:08:38,520 --> 00:08:41,620
You need not concern
yourselves with us, my friends.

115
00:08:43,700 --> 00:08:45,960
We are happy to let them sink.

116
00:08:46,860 --> 00:08:50,140
We do not require return
ships for this mission.

117
00:08:55,580 --> 00:08:57,140
We are off, Sir Luffy.

118
00:08:57,420 --> 00:09:00,480
I pray that we meet again soon. Stay well.

119
00:09:04,200 --> 00:09:05,217
This is it.

120
00:09:05,300 --> 00:09:06,740
Keep a low profile.

121
00:09:20,460 --> 00:09:22,880
What an inspiring sight to behold.

122
00:09:23,860 --> 00:09:26,680
Every last one of them, utterly resolute.

123
00:09:27,260 --> 00:09:29,320
No room for hesitation or doubt.

124
00:09:29,960 --> 00:09:31,080
It's win or die.

125
00:09:31,620 --> 00:09:34,796
They are challenging an
emperor of the sea, after all.

126
00:09:35,220 --> 00:09:37,632
Nothing less will suffice in this battle.

127
00:09:38,520 --> 00:09:39,350
What?

128
00:09:39,433 --> 00:09:41,137
What if they need to escape the island?

129
00:09:41,220 --> 00:09:43,808
Then they'll all be
swallowed up by the sea.

130
00:09:44,080 --> 00:09:45,440
Wait! Uh-oh!

131
00:09:45,760 --> 00:09:49,557
If they're sinking their ships, does
that mean we gotta sink the sun in?

132
00:09:49,640 --> 00:09:50,920
Over my dead body?

133
00:09:51,180 --> 00:09:53,356
We can hide a few ships, don't worry.

134
00:09:53,600 --> 00:09:56,188
But you should disembark,
it's time to move.

135
00:09:57,960 --> 00:09:59,520
Okie dokie, here we go!

136
00:10:02,740 --> 00:10:04,240
Wait, who are they?

137
00:10:05,080 --> 00:10:06,551
We're in trouble already.

138
00:10:07,020 --> 00:10:08,017
What's wrong, Carrot?

139
00:10:08,100 --> 00:10:09,357
The coast should be clear.

140
00:10:09,440 --> 00:10:10,675
But it isn't, though!

141
00:10:13,520 --> 00:10:14,920
How did we miss them?

142
00:10:15,080 --> 00:10:18,217
There's a whole ton of enemies
waiting right up the shore!

143
00:10:18,300 --> 00:10:20,124
Those aren't the beast pirates.

144
00:10:20,220 --> 00:10:21,050
Oh?

145
00:10:21,133 --> 00:10:23,058
You see the other end of the bridge?

146
00:10:33,160 --> 00:10:33,990
Hey!

147
00:10:34,073 --> 00:10:36,076
What the hell happened to my clothes?

148
00:10:37,200 --> 00:10:39,620
We look like beast pirates now.

149
00:10:42,080 --> 00:10:43,660
What the hell is this?

150
00:10:43,880 --> 00:10:46,115
That's my garb-garb special technique.

151
00:10:46,340 --> 00:10:49,940
What you see before you is known
as Teen's Clothing Company.

152
00:10:55,300 --> 00:10:59,320
I do not know you, but it seems
that you are mighty pirates indeed.

153
00:11:00,900 --> 00:11:04,257
I shall not dissuade you gentlemen
from invading this island,

154
00:11:04,340 --> 00:11:06,575
But know that the enemy is formidable.

155
00:11:06,980 --> 00:11:09,737
Furthermore, we are outnumbered
and we're five to one.

156
00:11:09,820 --> 00:11:13,938
So I advise you to take advantage
of those disguises I've constructed.

157
00:11:15,160 --> 00:11:16,320
Works for me.

158
00:11:16,620 --> 00:11:18,444
We're only interested in Kaido.

159
00:11:18,800 --> 00:11:21,565
The fewer lackeys we have
to fight, the better.

160
00:11:22,760 --> 00:11:24,620
Let's go. Yeah.

161
00:11:26,180 --> 00:11:27,500
This way, Sir Luffy.

162
00:11:28,100 --> 00:11:30,777
You and your crew should pass
through the gate as well.

163
00:11:30,860 --> 00:11:31,690
Awesome.

164
00:11:31,773 --> 00:11:33,092
This is going to be fun.

165
00:11:40,360 --> 00:11:42,020
Oh, here I go!

166
00:11:44,380 --> 00:11:45,220
Transform!

167
00:11:46,960 --> 00:11:50,160
Holy crap, beast mode! Yeah!

168
00:11:52,160 --> 00:11:54,820
Wow, Chobro, looking cool!

169
00:11:55,280 --> 00:11:56,600
Now it's my turn!

170
00:12:06,660 --> 00:12:11,020
You're a savage beauty, Nami,
the queen of the beasts! Mami!

171
00:12:11,780 --> 00:12:13,420
All right, let me try.

172
00:12:19,580 --> 00:12:21,540
How do I look, Robin?

173
00:12:21,760 --> 00:12:22,760
Am I beastly?

174
00:12:23,060 --> 00:12:24,180
You look normal.

175
00:12:25,240 --> 00:12:26,360
The savagery!

176
00:12:26,840 --> 00:12:28,557
You're taking this beastling too far.

177
00:12:28,640 --> 00:12:31,699
You look like you could rip
me in half in a hot way.

178
00:12:38,620 --> 00:12:39,450
Yay!

179
00:12:41,440 --> 00:12:42,270
Super!

180
00:12:43,320 --> 00:12:46,397
However, these clothes are
not made of traditional cloth.

181
00:12:46,480 --> 00:12:51,160
So if you take them off or they become
damaged, my technique will be dispelled.

182
00:12:54,580 --> 00:12:56,120
Heed my words, men.

183
00:12:57,060 --> 00:13:00,240
We tread upon Onigashima,
Kaido's stronghold.

184
00:13:00,700 --> 00:13:03,057
We must avoid unnecessary fights.

185
00:13:03,140 --> 00:13:06,880
Our destination is the
castle and the final battle!

186
00:13:09,420 --> 00:13:12,160
May Fortune walk beside us!

187
00:13:19,600 --> 00:13:23,280
I'm finally free from the ghost
of the accursed Kozuki clan!

188
00:13:23,580 --> 00:13:27,227
And I must say, in my whole life,
booze never tasted so sweet!

189
00:13:33,140 --> 00:13:35,780
Orochi is feeling carefree.

190
00:13:36,120 --> 00:13:37,880
His spy, Kanjuro,

191
00:13:38,120 --> 00:13:42,140
has faithfully told him every detail
of the Akazaya Samurai's plan.

192
00:13:42,420 --> 00:13:45,940
He believes he has completely
crushed their insurrection.

193
00:13:48,520 --> 00:13:51,280
Their rendezvous point is Tokage Porge!

194
00:13:51,600 --> 00:13:54,071
Destroy every last route that leads there!

195
00:14:00,960 --> 00:14:03,780
The Yakasaya samurai are helpless now!

196
00:14:03,980 --> 00:14:05,215
Time for them to die!

197
00:14:10,960 --> 00:14:15,100
His fears dispelled, he
celebrates his would-be victory.

198
00:14:18,640 --> 00:14:23,540
However, just outside the castle,
The raid is about to begin.

199
00:14:28,100 --> 00:14:30,940
The eastern forces are led by Kin'emon.

200
00:14:35,880 --> 00:14:38,960
The southern forces are led by Denjiro.

201
00:14:39,980 --> 00:14:43,120
Combined, there are
more than 5,000 troops.

202
00:14:52,500 --> 00:14:54,377
Nearby on Raw's submarine,

203
00:14:54,460 --> 00:14:58,297
the remaining Akazaya samurai make
their way to the rear of the island,

204
00:14:58,380 --> 00:15:02,100
aiming for the castle where
Kaido and Orochi are feasting.

205
00:15:06,040 --> 00:15:11,100
As over 5,000 troops draw ever
closer, the enemy remains unaware.

206
00:15:11,960 --> 00:15:13,900
Could you hurry it up, Franky?

207
00:15:14,660 --> 00:15:17,657
What the heck are you doing in
there that's taking so long?

208
00:15:17,740 --> 00:15:19,520
Everybody else already left.

209
00:15:20,140 --> 00:15:22,728
Can't rush genius, bro,
but don't you worry.

210
00:15:22,960 --> 00:15:25,040
We'll catch up in no time

211
00:15:52,860 --> 00:15:55,978
I saw that thing during the
battle on Fishman Island!

212
00:15:56,140 --> 00:15:58,580
Don't call my child a thing she made!

213
00:15:59,180 --> 00:16:00,740
It's Black Rhino, baby!

214
00:16:01,120 --> 00:16:03,355
And there's more where that came from!

215
00:16:11,500 --> 00:16:13,040
Rockio, take five!

216
00:16:13,360 --> 00:16:14,280
You're up!

217
00:16:20,420 --> 00:16:22,160
Take commander, Chobro!

218
00:16:22,940 --> 00:16:24,240
Reporting for duty!

219
00:16:25,380 --> 00:16:28,120
We're counting on you, pal! Look at that!

220
00:16:28,360 --> 00:16:29,997
Tough armor and a free ride!

221
00:16:30,080 --> 00:16:31,220
Own it, Chobro!

222
00:16:32,000 --> 00:16:34,460
I won't let you down! Nice!

223
00:16:35,360 --> 00:16:37,100
Let me handle the cannon!

224
00:16:39,440 --> 00:16:41,060
Chobro! Who's that?

225
00:16:42,000 --> 00:16:42,830
Franky!

226
00:16:43,920 --> 00:16:45,080
We're here!

227
00:16:46,680 --> 00:16:48,140
What do you say, gang?

228
00:16:48,260 --> 00:16:50,000
Is that worth the wait? Huh?

229
00:16:50,240 --> 00:16:53,040
Hey, where did Luffy
run off to? About that,

230
00:16:53,260 --> 00:16:55,677
he noticed Kid and his crew
going up the steps and got

231
00:16:55,760 --> 00:16:58,477
worried they might get in
the way of Kinemon's plan.

232
00:16:58,560 --> 00:17:02,120
Jaggy, I'm gonna shut your
butt down! Be back later!

233
00:17:04,420 --> 00:17:07,077
He's just gonna get in a
fight and make things worse!

234
00:17:07,160 --> 00:17:08,748
Why'd you let him get away?

235
00:17:09,060 --> 00:17:11,957
Zoro said exactly what you
said, then ran off too.

236
00:17:12,040 --> 00:17:14,897
He's just gonna get in a
fight and make things worse.

237
00:17:14,980 --> 00:17:16,156
Hey, Luffy, hold it!

238
00:17:17,980 --> 00:17:20,686
He'll just lose his way
and make things worse!

239
00:17:21,100 --> 00:17:21,980
Oh, I see.

240
00:17:22,680 --> 00:17:24,680
We can have fun without those two!

241
00:17:24,900 --> 00:17:29,380
Let's go for a romantic drive
through the battlefield, Nami-sweeet!

242
00:17:35,340 --> 00:17:36,300
Where the...?

243
00:17:37,420 --> 00:17:39,020
Let me take your place!

244
00:17:39,160 --> 00:17:41,160
You don't deserve to go to heaven!

245
00:17:41,820 --> 00:17:43,277
I don't know what to tell you, man.

246
00:17:43,360 --> 00:17:45,280
I'm a sharpshooter. Seeds taken!

247
00:17:50,520 --> 00:17:52,760
Hey, would a ride with me? Can I?

248
00:17:53,040 --> 00:17:53,980
I'd love to.

249
00:17:54,540 --> 00:17:57,080
Hang on, sir. Thank you. I will.

250
00:17:58,000 --> 00:17:59,180
You're not robbing!

251
00:17:59,440 --> 00:18:01,616
Nothing wrong with a little bromance.

252
00:18:03,020 --> 00:18:04,785
Guess I can't argue with that.

253
00:18:06,520 --> 00:18:08,080
Hey, Commander Chopper.

254
00:18:08,680 --> 00:18:10,717
We'll dock these at
the back of the island.

255
00:18:10,800 --> 00:18:11,976
I'll meet you there.

256
00:18:12,400 --> 00:18:13,580
Stay safe, bro.

257
00:18:14,100 --> 00:18:15,394
We're gonna dock them!

258
00:18:23,760 --> 00:18:30,200
Oh my goodness, I'll be
like a rock star again!

259
00:18:31,460 --> 00:18:34,320
You look like a bobblehead dog from hell!

260
00:18:35,160 --> 00:18:36,740
Let's go, Commander!

261
00:18:39,400 --> 00:18:40,437
Oh, Robin!

262
00:18:40,520 --> 00:18:42,320
Right up here with me!

263
00:18:42,980 --> 00:18:44,717
I think I'll pass, actually.

264
00:18:44,800 --> 00:18:47,859
The top of the tank is going
to get covered in dust.

265
00:18:49,060 --> 00:18:52,020
I suppose we'd better
start walking. Right.

266
00:18:57,060 --> 00:18:59,840
Looks like all of you
are as lively as ever.

267
00:19:00,100 --> 00:19:02,335
In a battle where everyone is excited,

268
00:19:02,480 --> 00:19:05,656
it's crucial to have someone
with a clear perspective.

269
00:19:05,780 --> 00:19:06,610
How mature.

270
00:19:06,880 --> 00:19:07,920
We appreciate it.

271
00:19:08,140 --> 00:19:09,964
I'm the new recruit, after all.

272
00:19:10,220 --> 00:19:11,691
I have to prove my worth.

273
00:19:20,440 --> 00:19:21,300
Come on.

274
00:19:21,580 --> 00:19:23,180
Don't force me to drag you.

275
00:19:26,200 --> 00:19:28,940
Kanjuro kidnapped Momonosuke and escaped,

276
00:19:29,080 --> 00:19:32,760
but has been met with one
obstacle after another ever since.

277
00:19:32,980 --> 00:19:36,420
As Kin'emon had hoped, he
has yet to make it to Orochi.

278
00:19:37,860 --> 00:19:40,137
I've never been down
in the tunnels before.

279
00:19:40,220 --> 00:19:42,573
I didn't know that they were so complex.

280
00:19:43,060 --> 00:19:45,597
The underlings still
think I'm with the enemy.

281
00:19:45,680 --> 00:19:48,617
They wouldn't believe me
if I told them the truth.

282
00:19:48,700 --> 00:19:53,229
It's going to be a disaster if those
samurai make it to the castle before me.

283
00:19:53,620 --> 00:19:56,208
One of these paths must
lead to Lord Orochi.

284
00:20:04,380 --> 00:20:06,040
My Commander Kaito!

285
00:20:06,200 --> 00:20:08,500
I'm ever, ever so happy to see you!

286
00:20:08,600 --> 00:20:10,541
Now you're just overcompensating.

287
00:20:15,320 --> 00:20:16,740
No one has drinks.

288
00:20:18,500 --> 00:20:21,441
Yeah, I didn't want to get
drunk with the lackeys.

289
00:20:21,800 --> 00:20:24,918
I was holding out till I
could drink with you, Kaido.

290
00:20:26,180 --> 00:20:27,440
Ah, fair enough.

291
00:20:27,980 --> 00:20:30,657
In that case, we can all
go to the hall later.

292
00:20:30,740 --> 00:20:32,800
No standing on ceremony today.

293
00:20:33,260 --> 00:20:35,837
Is there something we don't
know about going on right now?

294
00:20:35,920 --> 00:20:38,957
The plan was to introduce you to
Lin-Lin before we kick things off,

295
00:20:39,040 --> 00:20:40,897
but it seems she wants to make me wait.

296
00:20:40,980 --> 00:20:43,097
They said she's still getting dressed.

297
00:20:43,180 --> 00:20:44,945
Who knows when she'll be done.

298
00:20:45,420 --> 00:20:47,600
Anyway, Lin-Lin's not the issue here.

299
00:20:47,860 --> 00:20:49,680
A little complication came up.

300
00:20:49,900 --> 00:20:51,665
That's why I kept you waiting.

301
00:20:51,980 --> 00:20:54,240
Getting together already! No stopping!

302
00:20:54,600 --> 00:20:56,700
You can complain, if you like.

303
00:20:56,940 --> 00:21:00,737
But I'm not the one who called all
of you here in the first place.

304
00:21:00,820 --> 00:21:01,980
Huh? Alright.

305
00:21:02,380 --> 00:21:04,380
If it wasn't you, then who was it?

306
00:21:06,860 --> 00:21:07,740
I did.

307
00:21:08,360 --> 00:21:09,190
Huh?

308
00:21:09,660 --> 00:21:12,013
Sorry for going behind your back, Kaido.

309
00:21:12,200 --> 00:21:13,376
It was the only way.

310
00:21:13,700 --> 00:21:14,760
Should have known.

311
00:21:15,340 --> 00:21:17,217
King, this had better be worth it.

312
00:21:17,300 --> 00:21:18,130
Yeah, King.

313
00:21:18,240 --> 00:21:20,416
Why the hell did you go and trick us?

314
00:21:20,640 --> 00:21:24,917
Because some of you wouldn't have come
if you knew it was me who summoned you.

315
00:21:25,000 --> 00:21:26,880
Namely, who's who and Sasaki.

316
00:21:30,240 --> 00:21:31,180
That's true.

317
00:21:31,520 --> 00:21:34,597
You were both captains of
your own pirate crews once.

318
00:21:34,680 --> 00:21:38,597
So I'm sure you would want to take
our positions as lead performers.

319
00:21:38,680 --> 00:21:40,480
This is a meritocracy.

320
00:21:40,740 --> 00:21:42,093
What's wrong with that?

321
00:21:42,200 --> 00:21:43,906
Obviously, we're aiming high.

322
00:21:44,180 --> 00:21:45,380
Know your place.

323
00:21:46,060 --> 00:21:46,890
Whoa!

324
00:21:46,973 --> 00:21:48,100
I've heard enough.

325
00:21:48,480 --> 00:21:50,598
Can't you save this for another day?

326
00:21:50,700 --> 00:21:52,060
We're having a party.

327
00:21:53,400 --> 00:21:56,459
Well, King, you want to
tell us why you called them?

328
00:21:56,680 --> 00:22:01,340
Because I got tipped off about your
little complication, and I wanted to help.

329
00:22:01,540 --> 00:22:03,737
You could use their assistance, right?

330
00:22:03,820 --> 00:22:05,180
I suppose so.

331
00:22:06,700 --> 00:22:07,640
Ba Huang!

332
00:22:08,680 --> 00:22:09,800
Yes, sir!

333
00:22:22,720 --> 00:22:25,426
What's the schedule for
the rest of the night?

334
00:22:28,480 --> 00:22:32,520
Master Queen is currently performing
on the Golden Festival stage.

335
00:22:33,740 --> 00:22:36,397
However, once his performance is complete,

336
00:22:36,480 --> 00:22:39,537
The three lead performers and Fukurokuju

337
00:22:39,620 --> 00:22:43,940
will take to the stage and make a toast!

338
00:22:44,640 --> 00:22:50,100
Then, Lord Orochi and Commander
Kaido will give speeches!

339
00:22:50,880 --> 00:22:53,420
Next, the special guests will arrive.

340
00:22:53,840 --> 00:22:58,437
The Big Mom Pirates reach the
island on their ship and then...

341
00:22:58,520 --> 00:23:04,697
Commander Kaido and Big Mom will join
together and formally announce...

342
00:23:04,780 --> 00:23:07,960
The world's strongest pirate alliance

343
00:23:09,940 --> 00:23:12,580
Finally commander Kaido will make

344
00:23:18,200 --> 00:23:22,117
That is all an Important announcement.

345
00:23:22,200 --> 00:23:24,857
It's not like you to keep
us hanging like that.

346
00:23:24,940 --> 00:23:27,297
It's ever ever so annoying Yeah,

347
00:23:27,380 --> 00:23:31,920
I know I know but it'll cause
confusion if I say it now

348
00:23:33,380 --> 00:23:36,480
Anyway, let's talk about
that job I need you to do.

349
00:23:36,940 --> 00:23:40,080
My fool of a son Yamato disappeared today.

350
00:23:40,480 --> 00:23:43,500
Go find him and bring him back here.

351
00:23:44,340 --> 00:23:46,300
Oh my, that's not an easy task.

352
00:23:46,720 --> 00:23:48,777
Does that mean that your
mystery announcement

353
00:23:48,860 --> 00:23:51,507
has something to do with
young Master Yamato?

354
00:23:51,920 --> 00:23:53,600
Seems you're catching on.

355
00:23:53,940 --> 00:23:54,820
I see.

356
00:23:55,280 --> 00:23:57,809
Making us clean up your
family issues, huh?

357
00:23:59,560 --> 00:24:02,320
Okay, so what happens
if we bring him back?

358
00:24:02,640 --> 00:24:06,816
I'll give you the right to challenge
the lead performer of your choice.

359
00:24:07,340 --> 00:24:08,340
How's that?

360
00:24:09,100 --> 00:24:09,930
Seriously?

361
00:24:10,380 --> 00:24:11,840
Oh, I'll do it.

362
00:24:11,960 --> 00:24:12,980
Count me in.

363
00:24:13,120 --> 00:24:14,260
I got this.

364
00:24:14,940 --> 00:24:17,140
I assume you don't mind.

365
00:24:18,120 --> 00:24:19,540
No, not at all.

366
00:24:25,160 --> 00:24:26,277
Is that soup?

367
00:24:26,360 --> 00:24:28,380
Yeah, the chef made too much.

368
00:24:28,600 --> 00:24:30,517
Well, don't bring it here, stupid.

369
00:24:30,600 --> 00:24:31,877
Where should we put it?

370
00:24:31,960 --> 00:24:34,040
Come on, where are you?

371
00:24:34,740 --> 00:24:37,387
I bet you've never even
heard of Odin before.

372
00:24:37,620 --> 00:24:39,240
Don't you ruin this jaggy.

373
00:24:40,260 --> 00:24:43,600
Hey, have you seen a jaggy
in here? The what now?

374
00:24:44,060 --> 00:24:45,040
Is that food?

375
00:24:45,240 --> 00:24:46,946
That kind of food's no baker.

376
00:24:47,040 --> 00:24:48,020
Hold on.

377
00:24:48,740 --> 00:24:51,800
I got enough fans attracted to my...

378
00:24:52,660 --> 00:24:54,760
Think I'd run into balloons yet?

379
00:24:55,460 --> 00:24:56,640
Just showed up?

380
00:24:56,740 --> 00:24:58,020
Then grab a bitey!

381
00:24:58,880 --> 00:25:02,380
We got the goods right
there! All right! Hell yeah!

382
00:25:04,000 --> 00:25:06,837
You guys really know how
to chow down, don't you?

383
00:25:06,920 --> 00:25:08,637
Got more coming, help yourself!

384
00:25:08,720 --> 00:25:09,779
If you don't mind!

385
00:25:11,280 --> 00:25:13,337
That's what the Paradise Farm is for!

386
00:25:13,420 --> 00:25:14,832
Feeding us and us alone!

387
00:25:15,080 --> 00:25:19,786
If those rats from Okoboday Town ate
something this good, they'd die from shock!

388
00:25:19,900 --> 00:25:22,040
Just take the soup! I don't want it!

389
00:25:25,260 --> 00:25:26,090
It's...

390
00:25:28,020 --> 00:25:28,850
No!

391
00:25:29,180 --> 00:25:30,010
No!

392
00:25:30,093 --> 00:25:30,923
Hot, hot, hot, hot!

393
00:25:31,006 --> 00:25:31,836
What the hell, dude?

394
00:25:31,919 --> 00:25:32,997
Why did you bring Oshiniko?

395
00:25:33,080 --> 00:25:35,668
We're doing drinks and
appetizers right now!

396
00:25:36,740 --> 00:25:37,570
Oshiniko?

397
00:25:37,653 --> 00:25:38,483
Don't blame me.

398
00:25:38,566 --> 00:25:40,977
They made too much, so
they're passing it off on us.

399
00:25:41,060 --> 00:25:41,942
We're drinking!

400
00:25:42,140 --> 00:25:44,057
You think this pairs with alcohol?

401
00:25:44,140 --> 00:25:46,317
We got plenty of better things to eat.

402
00:25:46,400 --> 00:25:47,520
Forget this crap.

403
00:25:47,700 --> 00:25:49,657
It's so sweet, it makes my teeth ache!

404
00:25:49,740 --> 00:25:52,400
Why don't you spill it over Okobore town?

405
00:25:53,240 --> 00:25:56,260
They'll lick it off the
ground and thank us for it!

406
00:26:13,280 --> 00:26:14,110
YUMMY!

407
00:26:16,380 --> 00:26:20,220
I had no idea that food
could taste so good! Huh?

408
00:26:20,440 --> 00:26:22,997
Does that mean you've never
had this stuff before?

409
00:26:23,080 --> 00:26:25,374
It's even got little mochi balls in it!

410
00:26:25,520 --> 00:26:27,402
This is the feast of a lifetime!

411
00:26:37,800 --> 00:26:40,900
I wish I could eat food
like this every day!

412
00:26:44,160 --> 00:26:45,200
Filthy beggars!

413
00:26:45,380 --> 00:26:47,580
Even our trash is too good for you!

414
00:26:52,640 --> 00:26:55,440
Thank you.

415
00:27:19,600 --> 00:27:22,120
Thank you.
